nations of kang the  conqueror or in mcu terms he who remains  who fans met in the loki series as a  time traveler kang has a long and  complicated history ramitat is one of  the many personas he's adopted during  his infinite quest to control time  throughout the series there are multiple  hints that mark was somehow involved in  the murder of leyla's father layla  naturally presses mark to find out the  truth which is finally revealed when  mark says my partner got greedy in me  [Music]  he executed everyone at dick's site  viewers later learned what comics fans  already knew that mark's partner was a  vicious killer named raul bushman pretty  much everything we see in the show is  right out of the comics when mark tried  to stop bushmen from murdering a group  of archaeologists bushman shot mark and  left him for dead leading to konchu's  intervention and the creation of moon  knight there is one difference though in  the comics mark's lover is called  marlene the show took marlene's  backstory including mark's involvement  in the death of her father and used it  to create the new character of leila  abdallah al fuli given how much his  relationship with mark has been set up  chances seem pretty high that we'll  eventually see bushmen in the tv show  whether or not we'll see the gruesome  end of their rivalry remains to be seen  as in the comics moon knight killed him  by cutting his face off that doesn't  sound very disney  after mark spector is shot by harrow he  falls into a pool of water he wakes up  in what appears to be some sort of  asylum complete with bingo orderlies  what looks like an authentic marvel moon  knight action figure as well as plenty  of familiar faces and a drawing of  konshu there are many things present to  convince steven that everything he  thought had been going on for the last  four episodes didn't happen but the best  may be tombuster this fake vhs tape is a  mixture of indiana jones and tomb raider  a low budget title that our hero could  be pulling his fantasies from with the  appropriate amount of cheesy dialogues  sets and knock-off music at least now we  know what happened to paulman tobin  yes  and to anyone who chooses a path of  greed  it's a clever setup a brilliant change  of pace and allows ethan hawk to channel  carl jung who the actor told  entertainment weekly helped guide his  portrayal of the asylum version of  harrow what viewers may not know though  is that this setting was inspired by the  2016 comic story moon knight lunatic  which put mark in this exact position to  examine his grasp on reality  in the final moments of episode 4 mark  spector and steven grant are surprised  to run into a giant hippopotamus and who  can blame them hi  it may be a giant anthropomorphic  creature dressed in ancient egyptian  garb but considering their current  situation her appearance turns out to be  a blessing this is taweret the egyptian  goddess of childbirth and fertility as  much as her appearance might have been a  surprise to some viewers it was actually  set up in the first episode while  working in the museum gift shop donna  asks grant to grab a box of stuffed  hippos which leads him to offering some  unwanted info on who taweret is it's a  small reference that also helps to show  off more of our hero's vast egyptian  knowledge and this little tidbit makes  for an entertaining note during a  re-watch  part of episode 5 sees taweret the hippo  goddess acting as a sort of post-life  tour guide for mark and steven after  some joint yelling the two begin to  realize that this depiction of putnam  medical facility called putnam  psychiatric hospital in the comics where  mark spector was sent as a kid is  actually a part of their journey through  the afterlife but the hospital itself  isn't the only easter egg during the  conversation taweret mentions that there  are other versions of the afterlife as  well you'd be surprised how many  intersectional planes of untethered  consciousness exist yeah ah like the  ancestral plane oh just gorgeous  this isn't just another part of egyptian  mythology she's praising however but the  ancestral plane from the black panther  film this is a fun line that brings moon  knight a bit closer to the mcu proper it  makes perfect sense that taweret would  mention it as well considering her  connection to bast who in egyptian  mythology was a cat goddess and in the  mcu is the panther goddess of wakanda we  mostly see it as a place where the  various black panthers journey to speak  to the dead and seek wisdom but there is  potentially much more that could be done  with this realm if marvel ever wanted to  do a small crossover into the afterlife  shown at the end of moon night  in episode 5 mark spector and steven  grant attempt to balance their scales  and that means exploring several deep  memories and facing some harsh truths  about their past part of this is  learning about the death of a boy  affectionately called roro who is  actually randall rand spector mark's  younger brother in this mcu version of  moon knight mark is blamed for the  unexpected accident that takes his  brother's life things are somehow even  worse in the comics though in the show  mark's mother accuses him of being  jealous of his younger sibling but it's  the other way around in the source  material rand doesn't die as a child but  instead grows up to be an insane serial  killer supervillain called hatchet man  who is obsessed with destroying his  older brother mark rand eventually  becomes a twisted mirror of moon knight  called shadow knight and the punisher is  forced to kill him to end his reign of  terror does rand's rich comic history  imply that the mcu version may have  somehow survived given that ancient gods  brought mark back from the dead twice  during the course of the show  anything is possible  as mark and stephen journey through  their collective mind we are shown  several interesting things but most of  the heart catch references were in their  childhood room much of the bedroom is  set up purposefully to look as did in  the run of comics by jeff lemire and  greg smallwood this includes the race  car bed and a specific poster on the  wall for star wars episode 4 a new hope  which doubles as a nod to actor oscar  isaac being a part of the franchise in  the newest trilogy there are also toys  lying around pictures on the walls and a  cubs banner to let everyone know we're  in chicago but a couple of things may  have gone unnoticed the item that comes  into focus first is the name bluebird on  the wing of an airplane which some comic  book scholars think may reference an  obscure spider-man character though it's  possibly just a coincidence however in  that same shot we get our first glance  at the many astronaut figures that the  imaginative young hero has this is  likely another comic reference to  another personality of marx who was an  astronaut that fought werewolves  which might sound like an odd  combination but astronaut werewolves are  surprisingly common in the marvel  universe also more simply astronauts go  to the moon and moon knight is well you  get the idea finally just below the  scales in mark's room another recurring  motif throughout the show is a pair of  grey nunchaku in the comics the fist of  konshu originally uses a truncheon to  fight with which he first modifies for  use as nunchaku in the 1980 issue moon  knight number two these are a couple of  nice subtle nods that don't feel out of  place in the childhood memory and may  have helped influence mark's future  adventures  there's so much to see in young mark's  bedroom but one thing in particular  stands out that was made just for the  show the tomb buster poster if you look  closely you can see a couple fun things  on it doug purlin is the name given to  the lead actor for tombuster which is a  clever homage to moon knight's creators  doug mensch and don perlin and the  poster also shows that the film was  presented by timely atlas studios which  is another instance of two names timely  comics and atlas comics shoved together  timely is what marvel comics was known  as in the 1940s while atlas is what they  were called in the 1950s it's an  extremely deep cut for most viewers but  that poster also begs to be stared at so  it works out  before the show's release many viewers  were wondering about whether or not this  iteration of moon knight in the mcu  would remain jewish as he is in the  comics his heritage and religion are a  key part of mark spector especially  since his father was a rabbi it's a deep  part of the character and important for  representation thankfully there was some  hope given to those who wanted to see  this mentioned in the series when  director muhammad diob posted on twitter  that fans who were curious about that  aspect of the character would be pleased  and they were while in the asylum going  through their memories mark and steven  must discuss their mother's death which  brings up the line dad called me after  all these years  about her shiva and i couldn't  i couldn't do it  in judaism shiva is the first seven days  of mourning the observance of which is  sometimes referred to as sitting shiva  in english plus when the two characters  revisit this specific memory we also see  mark dressed in all black wearing a  yamaka these elements give the audience  insights into mark's religious  background and acknowledge his following  of the traditions all while mark and  steven are dealing with the weight of  their own present death  just as mark and steven begin working  together and find their balance one of  them has to go and get thrown overboard  during the fight at the end of episode 5  steven taps into the side of mark that  can wield a bat just before he throws  himself into helping mark a bit too much  and hits the sands at first he tries to  catch up with the boat but steven is  quickly overcome by sans freezing him  there it's a sad scene that comes just  when things are looking up but we all  should have seen it coming because it  was actually teased right at the start  of the series in the first episode when  stephen grant is still blissfully  ignorant of his other life he shows off  his knowledge in the museum where he  works he speaks to a young girl about  pyramids death and being judged only for  her to come back at him with a couple of  confusing questions including and did it  suck for you getting rejected from the  field of reads what if that makes sense  because i'm not dead am i  stephen is understandably confused but  now we know that the child was either  aware of his future or perhaps just a  bit cruel  we all knew layla was destined for great  things but the season one moon knight  finale nearly outdoes itself in that  regard when layla unexpectedly becomes a  superhero herself after rejecting the  offer to become the avatar of konshu she  instead becomes an avatar of taweret  after harrow attempts to bury her inside  the pyramid laila is seen bursting  through the wall in a glorious new  costume she wastes no time with her  newfound powers fighting by her  husband's side and saving lives after  she rescues one group an awestruck girl  asks the new avatar if she's an egyptian  superhero and it's a big moment for a  lot of people  it wasn't really unexpected though as  there were hints throughout including  konchu calling her a quote little bug  that's significant because layla may or  may not be a version of the comic  character scarlet scarab in the comics  the scarlet scarab is an egyptian  superhero identity taken on by a father  and son duo named faul naturally fans  connected the dots between the scarlet  scarab and this new mcu hero embodied by  leila elfuli however there are some  differences as the comics version of  scarlet scarab is not connected to  tawere but rather gets his powers from  an ancient magical artifact moon knight  director mohammed diov has been coy  about whether or not leila is  technically scarlet scarab telling  collider that while unofficially she is  the scarlet scarab they intentionally  left it vague so they could officially  decide later on set we were calling her  scarlet scarab i would love to keep it  open because i don't know how things are  going to go i'd rather keep it open for  her  the post-credits scene in the season  finale of moon knight pleased many fans  with the final reveal of the jake  lockley personality as well as the  comics accurate depictions of the white  limo complete with spectre vanity plates  and conscious crisp suit but there's  another fun easter egg that avid readers  would have spotted the name of the  facility that arthur harrow has been  abducted from is the cenkevich  psychiatric hospital named after  renowned comic book artist bilson kevich  cinkevich is a prolific and  revolutionary artist known for his  uncommon style and methods of blending  in traits from other practitioners of  the craft sim cabbage not only worked on  the first moon night book in 1980 but he  provided many great covers and insides  for the hero for years afterward in fact  many believe that the character of moon  knight owes much of its success to  sankevich it seems fitting that the show  which will hopefully help mark and  company to continue to grow with more  new fans pays tribute to him in a fun  way during the final scene check out one  of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite shows are coming soon subscribe  to our youtube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

